AUDIO: '4K 60 frames per second so we can slow it down by 50% in editing to get the slow motion shots. And then in the settings, we\'re going to be using a flat color profile called'

[02:18] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'i-log. &gt;&gt; Mhm. &gt;&gt; And this records footage with no contrast, color, or sharpness. And then professionals like to color grade their footage in editing after because we want to make the footage straight out the'

[02:31] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'camera ready to upload onto social media so we don\'t have to do any of that in editing. We\'re going to use a filter called Leica natural, which is going to apply the color, the contrast, and sharpness for'

[02:43] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'us. And it\'s going to look really nice. And then in the exposure settings, I will set the ISO to 100 because it\'s a bright sunny day. &gt;&gt; Mhm. &gt;&gt; The EV is set to minus 0.3 so we protect the bright parts of the video. And the'

[02:56] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'shutter speed is set to auto because we\'re moving in between shade and brighter areas. So we\'re going to let the camera adjust automatically. And then we don\'t need to worry about these settings again when shooting throughout'

[03:08] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the day. The white balance is set to 5600 Kelvin. This is the best setting in a bright sunny day like this. So this will keep the footage not too cool or too warm. It\'ll make sure it\'s natural. The'

[03:20] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'metering mode I like to keep on matrix. The focus mode will be autofocus mode so it will hunt focus automatically. And I\'m going to leave breathing compensation off. So if you wave your hand in front of your face, you\'ll'

